course: dictionary
lesson: 8470
title: Salt: what it is and what it does
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Salt is a small white grain that makes food taste salty. It can come from the sea or from rock under the ground. «Salt is spread on icy roads» to help stop ice forming.
explain: Salt is also a verb and an adjective. To salt is to put salt on food or on roads, and salty describes something that tastes of salt. Read the words around it to see which one it is.
explain: In science, salt has a special meaning. «Salt dissolves in water», which means it breaks up and mixes in so you cannot see it. When seawater evaporates, the water goes into the air and the salt is left behind.
explain: Salt also appears in sayings. If you «take it with a pinch of salt», you do not believe it fully. If someone is «worth his salt», he is good at his job. The context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Salt is made of sodium and chlorine.
fact: Salt lowers the freezing point of water, so salty water freezes at a lower temperature than plain water.
fact: Gritters spread salt on roads before a frost, so ice forms less easily.
fact: Salt from sea spray or gritted roads makes iron rust faster, so cars and railings by the sea rust quickly.
fact: Too much salt in your food is bad for your health.
exercise: Why do gritters spread salt on icy roads before a frost? | *Because salty water freezes at a lower temperature, so ice forms less easily | To make the road taste nicer | To paint lines on the road | To make the road turn green
exercise: «Salt dissolves in water.» What does dissolves mean here? | Turns into a bigger lump | *Breaks up and mixes in so you cannot see it | Makes a loud fizz | Floats on top like oil
exercise: In «take it with a pinch of salt», what does the speaker mean? | Keep it safe from the rain | The idea is very tasty | Eat a tiny amount of salt | *Do not believe it fully
test: What is salt made of? | *Sodium and chlorine | Carbon and oxygen | Sugar and water | Iron and rust
test: «Salty water freezes at a lower temperature than pure water.» What does this help with? | Making ice cream | Making bread rise | Cooking pasta faster | *Stopping ice forming on roads
exam: Which sentence uses salt as a verb, meaning to put salt on something? | Salt is a white grain that comes from the sea. | *The gritter will salt the icy road before dawn. | Table salt is sodium chloride. | The salt dissolved in the water.
